---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Python Under the Hood: how the interactive lessons work, credits, license, and how your progress is stored.">
  <div class="prose" style="padding-top:2rem">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Python Under the Hood is a free, interactive course. You read short lessons, run and edit every example in a
      real Python interpreter in your browser (<a href="https://pyodide.org">Pyodide</a>, CPython compiled to
      WebAssembly), then check what you learned with quizzes and auto-graded exercises.
    </p>

    <h2>Credits</h2>
    <p>
      The course structure (four parts and their sections and lectures) follows <strong>Dr. Fred Baptiste's</strong>
      <em>Python 3: Deep Dive</em> series on Udemy:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/python-3-deep-dive-part-1/">Part 1: Functional</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/python-3-deep-dive-part-2/">Part 2: Iteration, Generators</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/python-3-deep-dive-part-3/">Part 3: Hash Maps</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/python-3-deep-dive-part-4/">Part 4: OOP</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Code examples are adapted from his <a href="https://github.com/fbaptiste/python-deepdive">python-deepdive</a>
      repository. Lesson text, diagrams, quizzes and exercises are original to this site. Examples are updated for
      modern Python (3.13) where behavior has changed since the videos were recorded.
    </p>

    <h2 id="license">License</h2>
    <p>
      The python-deepdive repository is licensed under the
      <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html">GNU General Public License v3.0</a>. This site, including
      its adapted code, is distributed under the same license (GPL-3.0-or-later).
    </p>

    <h2>Your progress</h2>
    <p>
      Completed lectures, quiz scores and exercise drafts are stored only in your browser (localStorage). Your
      progress and code are never sent to a server. Clearing your browser's site data resets your progress.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      To learn which lessons are useful, this site uses <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel
      Web Analytics</a>, which counts page views anonymously. It uses no cookies and doesn't track you across sites.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
